{
  "dom_id": "question-167644",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "What was the exact rate of change of the profits' value at month $4?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\,$ thousand dollars per month.",
  "worked_solution": "The function ${f}^{′}(x)$ models the rate of change of the value of the profits, applicable in the domain of $f(x).$\n\nThus, the rate of change of the value of the profit at $x=4$ months is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(4) & =\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the profits was $\\frac{1}{3}$ thousand dollars per month.",
